:: Darius Desk Numbers [micro_event event nobr] {"position":"1550,3275","size":"100,100"}
/* Desk visitor (micro event 36, "A normal workday" in Define Events): $darius ran the numbers on our own office,
   and they are too good. A week after Too Much Work, once ($flags.dariusAskedAboutNumbers). Shown in the CMD drawer,
   so no action is spent and there is no exit link. */
<<set $flags.dariusAskedAboutNumbers to true>>
<p>$darius.name puts the printout down in front of me and turns it so it faces the right way. One chart, two lines. One of them is labeled <i>benchmark</i>. The other one isn't labeled at all, and it sits a long way above the first.</p>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
	{ who: $darius, text: "Do you have five minutes? It concerns us rather than a client, which is why I didn't want to put it in an email." },
	{ who: $player, text: "Sure, go ahead." },
	{ who: $darius, text: "I've been tracking our own output: closed tickets, hardware revisions, report turnaround. Measured against teams of comparable size and funding, we're thirty-eight percent above where we ought to be, and I checked the benchmark three different ways to make sure I wasn't flattering us." },
	{ who: $player, text: "So... we're good?" },
	{ who: $darius, text: "We're anomalous, which isn't quite the same thing. Nobody has called in sick, nobody is ever late, and $ethan.name closed more tickets this month than in the whole of his last job. He told me that himself, and he seemed slightly alarmed by it." },
	{ who: $darius, text: "I'd like to run a proper study: hours, desk positions, lighting, air quality, who sits near whom. If the effect turns out to be reproducible, it's worth more than anything currently in our pipeline." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<p>Air quality. He puts it in the middle of the list with no particular weight on it, and I catch myself studying his face, trying to tell whether that was on purpose. I honestly can't.</p>
<br>
<div id="darius-numbers-choice" class="choices">
	<div>
		<<link "Credit the team">>
			<<replace "#darius-numbers-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "Honestly? I think it's just the team. We're small, everybody owns their stuff, nobody can hide in meetings... that kind of thing." },
					{ who: $darius, text: "That's a cultural explanation. In my experience, those are what people offer when nothing has been measured yet." },
					{ who: $player, text: "Then maybe measure something a client is paying for? I'd rather have you on that." },
					{ text: "He smiles a little. I don't think I dressed that no up nearly as well as I meant to." },
					{ who: $darius, text: "Understood. I'll put it aside." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>He picks up the printout and goes back to his desk. He doesn't throw it away. I watch him slide it into the leather folder he carries home every evening, between two client reports, very neatly.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "Efficiency" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<div>
		<<link "Make it a sales slide">>
			<<replace "#darius-numbers-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "You know what, make it a slide. Thirty-eight percent more output, clients love a number they can repeat at dinner." },
					{ who: $darius, text: "That isn't quite what the data says, though. It says our team produces more, and as far as I'm aware, we don't use our own product in here." },
					{ who: $player, text: "We, uh... we kind of do. We've sort of been the pilot site since we moved in." },
					{ text: "He goes very still for a moment, the way he does when a column doesn't add up and he's working out which cell lied to him." },
					{ who: $darius, text: "Then I'd want to see the logs." },
					{ who: $player, text: "I can get you a summary." },
					{ who: $darius, text: "A summary. Of course." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>He says it the way other people say 'sure you did'. Two days later the slide shows up in our client deck anyway, clean and convincing, with a footnote in very small type that reads <i>internal pilot, n = 1</i>.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "Reputation" 2>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
</div>
